---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Timeline confirmed by Chris: 9-12 months (matches the brochure).
const myths = [
  ['Modular is a budget option', 'For an architect-designed home, modular is often the more economical path. Compared with a custom home of similar design and finish, a ma home is comparable in cost and in most cases less expensive. Because the work is done in a factory, there are fewer variables like weather delays to put the budget at risk. A basic tract home will still cost less, but it is a different product.'],
  ['Modular doesn’t save much time', 'Modular builds in about 50–60% of the time of a conventional home. The modules are built in a factory over a few weeks while the foundation and site work move ahead, and set in days. Start to move-in is typically 9 to 12 months, because permits, financing, utilities and finishing work take the same time they do for any home.'],
  ['Modular is simpler, or modular is harder', 'It is still a construction project, and it goes more smoothly. Often more than half of the scope of work takes place in the factory, in a controlled setting with materials ordered ahead. We coordinate the many people involved so you do not have to.'],
  ['Modular is flimsy', 'A ma home is built to be as solid as any site-built home, if not stronger. We build to the modular code on permanent foundations, to IRC standards. Each module is engineered to withstand transportation and being lifted by a crane.'],
  ['Modular is not green', 'Modular is efficient from the start. Our standard specs include 2x6 walls (R-19 insulation), thermally broken windows, low-VOC finishes and tankless water heaters. Solar panels, rainwater collection and geothermal systems are available as upgrades, mostly installed on site. If there is a sustainability benchmark you want to hit, we can hit it.'],
];
---
<Base title="Myths" description="Myths and facts about modular construction: cost, speed, simplicity, strength and sustainability.">
  <div class="wrap page-title"><h1>Myths</h1><p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">A few ideas about modular construction are worth clearing up. Here is what we have learned over our almost two decades building ma homes.</p></div>
  <div class="wrap section" style="padding-top:8px">
    <div class="myths">
      {myths.map((m, i) => (
        <>
          <div class="myth"><h3>Myth: {m[0]}</h3><p><strong>Fact:</strong> {m[1]}</p>{i === 0 && <img src="/images/site/living-room.webp" alt="Living room of a ma modular home with sliding glass doors to the deck" width="1091" height="960" data-zoom loading="lazy" />}</div>
        </>
      ))}
      <div class="myth photo"><img src="/images/site/living-detail.webp" alt="Interior detail of a ma modular living room" width="960" height="1119" data-zoom loading="lazy" /></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
